  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 5.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.54,
      "end_seconds": 12.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.42,
      "end_seconds": 24.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.22,
      "text": "good afternoon doctor i look after them so so I thought I'd come yeah doctor it's breathlessness on exertion that's what we're worried about"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.58,
      "end_seconds": 33.14,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "So, what's the timeline, when did it begin? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.75,
      "end_seconds": 39.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "I've had it for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.78,
      "end_seconds": 43.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "how much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.69,
      "end_seconds": 47.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "it's mild, honestly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.44,
      "end_seconds": 51.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.72,
      "end_seconds": 57.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "it it happens a few times a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.94,
      "end_seconds": 64.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 64.89,
      "end_seconds": 70.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Actually tell the doctor about the other thing that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.55,
      "end_seconds": 88.26,
      "duration_seconds": 13.71,
      "text": "erm, um, I was getting to that! Right, um, I've had a heavy feeling in the left arm too, for four weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.76,
      "end_seconds": 96.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Rate it it for me mild moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.35,
      "end_seconds": 100.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "it's severe, honestly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.62,
      "end_seconds": 106.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Have you had tightness in your chest when you walk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.61,
      "end_seconds": 108.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "Mm, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.42,
      "end_seconds": 112.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.12,
      "end_seconds": 114.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "It's mild honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.26,
      "end_seconds": 121.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "mm, okay have you had breathlessness on exertion before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.95,
      "end_seconds": 131.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "Yes something like this happened last winter and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.86,
      "end_seconds": 136.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "a few quick ones: palpitations or swelling in the ankles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.84,
      "end_seconds": 142.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Let me think, no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.54,
      "end_seconds": 146.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "mm-hmm have you noticed fever cough or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.21,
      "end_seconds": 150.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.69,
      "end_seconds": 154.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.76,
      "end_seconds": 159.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "that's normal as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.14,
      "end_seconds": 168.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "okay, have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.0,
      "end_seconds": 173.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "okay, so no, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.78,
      "end_seconds": 178.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.99,
      "end_seconds": 185.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "yes, I had my womb taken out, fifteen years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.64,
      "end_seconds": 189.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.95,
      "end_seconds": 199.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "it's a... um, uh, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.77,
      "end_seconds": 203.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.45,
      "end_seconds": 229.24,
      "duration_seconds": 24.79,
      "text": "right, for my cholesterol, I believe my husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given i'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day hmm, I'm on telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 231.12,
      "end_seconds": 240.12,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "It's meant to be once a day though I don't see she take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.98,
      "end_seconds": 246.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "I take aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.81,
      "end_seconds": 250.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "right, do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.41,
      "end_seconds": 267.51,
      "duration_seconds": 16.1,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol, for five years. Okay, so I've had diabetes, yes. It's the not knowing that gets to me. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. Yes, heart disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.74,
      "end_seconds": 269.44,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.99,
      "end_seconds": 273.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.84,
      "end_seconds": 283.71,
      "duration_seconds": 9.87,
      "text": "so, yes, heart disease and high blood pressure are known to us, good to have that clear. Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.89,
      "end_seconds": 289.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.38,
      "end_seconds": 296.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "so, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.86,
      "end_seconds": 306.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "yes, cat fur, it gives me wheezing so, yes, grass pollen, it gives me sneezing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.33,
      "end_seconds": 311.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.66,
      "end_seconds": 321.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "bear with me while this finishes.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.07,
      "end_seconds": 344.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 92 temperature is 36.4 degrees blood pressure 148 over 101."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.85,
      "end_seconds": 368.43,
      "duration_seconds": 13.58,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. The most likely explanation is angina-type chest pain. I can't rule out a musculoskeletal cause yet. Gastro-oesophageal reflux is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.82,
      "end_seconds": 375.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Okay, so is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.98,
      "end_seconds": 385.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now angina-type chest pain is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.83,
      "end_seconds": 405.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "let's get an echocardiogram, for chest tightness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 407.03,
      "end_seconds": 411.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "I can book that for Monday at 3:30 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.9,
      "end_seconds": 445.76,
      "duration_seconds": 33.86,
      "text": "I want an ECG done that's for chest tightness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. The treatment will be GTN spray 0.4 milligrams when the chest tightness comes as needed. That should help with chest tightness. Don't push through the chest tightness stop sit down and use the spray if I've given it to you. If it hasn't settled next month we'd think about a treadmill test but not now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 447.3,
      "end_seconds": 455.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "I'd like you back after the results are back that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 457.42,
      "end_seconds": 459.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}